  "descriptionRussian": "Сравнение с помощью прилагательных",
  "imageName": "arrow.up.arrow.down",
  "intro": "To compare things in Russian, use the comparative form. There are two types: simple (synthetic) comparatives add -ее/-ей or have irregular forms, and compound comparatives use более + adjective. Simple comparatives are invariable (don't decline!). Use чем (than) or the genitive case for comparison: Он выше, чем я. / Он выше меня. (He is taller than me.) Many common adjectives have irregular comparatives you must memorize.",
  "rules": [
    "Simple comparatives (лучше, больше, интереснее) never change form — they are invariable regardless of gender, number, or case.",
    "Two ways to say 'than': use чем + nominative (старше, чем брат) or just genitive (старше брата) — both are equally correct.",
    "Memorize the four most common irregulars first: лучше (better), хуже (worse), больше (bigger), меньше (smaller).",
    "Use более + adjective (compound comparative) when you need the comparative to decline: более интересная книга (a more interesting book)."
  ],
  "examples": [
    "Эта книга интереснее. (This book is more interesting.)",
    "Он выше, чем я. (He is taller than me.), with чем",
    "Она старше меня. (She is older than me.), with genitive",
    "Сегодня лучше, чем вчера. (Today is better than yesterday.)"
  ],
